		// => (i+1)*dp[i] = sum_{j=0}^{i-1} dp[j] + dp[i]
		// => i*dp[i] = sum_{j=0}^{i-1} dp[j]
		// But sum_{j=0}^{i-1} dp[j] = i * dp[i-1] (from the equation for i-1)
		// So i*dp[i] = i*dp[i-1]
		// => dp[i] = dp[i-1]
		// That can't be right. Let me check with the sample.
		// For p=2, e=1, k=1:
		// dp[1] = (dp[0]) / 2 = 0
		// But the expected value of 2^exponent is 2^0 * 1/2 + 2^1 * 1/2 = 1/2 + 1 = 3/2
